        Root cause:
        The bug is caused by the introduction of the MPM (Multi-Processor Management) interrupt controller in the device tree configuration for the MSM8996 platform. This configuration leads to crashes during bootup, particularly when probing IOMMUs, likely due to incorrect handling or initialization of interrupts associated with the MPM, which interferes with the system's ability to boot properly.

        Commit message:
        Revert "arm64: dts: qcom: msm8996: Hook up MPM"

Commit 09896da07315 ("arm64: dts: qcom: msm8996: Hook up MPM") has
hooked up the MPM irq chip on the MSM8996 platform. However this causes
my Dragonboard 820c crash during bootup (usually when probing IOMMUs).
Revert the offending commit for now. Quick debug shows that making
tlmm's wakeup-parent point to the MPM is enough to trigger the crash.

